This mutation makes movement toward the goals respect nearby enemies. `progress` now penalises destination tiles within 2 of an enemy, and `score` scales the resulting gain by 10 so a move is worth taking only when it still closes distance on a safe tile. This costs one `enemies()` call per candidate move, so it is the fuel risk to watch.

```python
@gene("s4", "distance gained toward goals, minus a penalty for ending next to enemies", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    d = at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t)
    near = sum(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, t) <= 2)
    return 3 * d - 4 * near

